# Dependencies are vendored and committed (go mod vendor).
# No network needed after clone.

# Build artifacts
/bin/
/ze
/ze-*
/functional
# cache/ is a SYMLINK to the durable cache (~/.cache/ze), created by
# scripts/dev/ensure-links.py. tmp/ is a real scratch dir by default; the tracked tmp/go.mod
# sentinel keeps `go list ./...` from descending into the Go/QEMU caches under it. After the
# opt-in `make ze-migrate-scratch`, tmp/ becomes a symlink to $TMPDIR/ze/<checkout-id>, which
# `go list` skips without a sentinel. See plan/spec-relocate-scratch-and-cache.md.
/cache
tmp/*
!tmp/go.mod

# go test -c / benchmark binaries
*.test

# Build outputs (kernel, initrd, pxe, ipxe)
build/

# credentials database (generated by ze init)
database.zefs
etc/ze/database.zefs*

# Functional tests under development. A .ci in here is invisible to every suite
# and every repo-wide gate (see test/draft/README.md), so a half-written test can
# never redden `make ze-verify` or CI. Ignored rather than merely excluded: CI
# checks out git, so an ignored tree does not exist there at all, which makes the
# guarantee independent of every gate remembering to skip it.
# Promote with: mv test/draft/<suite>/<name>.ci test/<suite>/<name>.ci
#
# `test/draft/*`, NOT `test/draft/`: git does not descend into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so the negation below would never be evaluated and the README would
# be ignored too, leaving the convention undiscoverable from a fresh clone.
test/draft/*
!test/draft/README.md

# MRT data files (large, downloaded)
test/internet/*.gz
test/internet/*.bz2
test/internet/*.tmp

# Research output (large generated files)
docs/research/comparison/
docs/research/ze-vpp-plan.md
*-inlined.html

# Coverage reports
coverage.out
coverage.html

# Mutation testing incremental cache (gomu hardcodes this cwd path)
.gomu_history.json

# Python
__pycache__/

# Zeledon weekly-update Discord archive: authoritative copy of the text is the
# published website (gh-pages/changes/posts/), so the local archive is kept only
# for post_weekly.py's already-posted skip check, not committed.
scripts/zeledon/weekly/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Obsidian
.obsidian/

# Claude session state (lives in tmp/session/, covered by tmp/ ignore)
# Legacy locations kept for transition period:
.claude/session-state.md
.claude/session-state-*.md
.claude/.session-*
.claude/.compaction-detected
.claude/.compaction-detected-*
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Generated AI tool config (canonical sources: ai/skills/, ai/INSTRUCTIONS.md)
# Regenerate with: make ze-ai-sync
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.claude/skills/
.codex/skills/
.agents/skills/

test/perf/results/
bin/ze-perf-linux
# Cross-compiled ze binary staged into the ipsec-interop Docker build context by
# test/ipsec-interop/run.py (regenerated each run; ~58MB, must not be committed).
test/ipsec-interop/ze-linux
# ze.conf with %%PKI_DIR%% resolved to a container path, written by lab.py per run.
test/ipsec-interop/scenarios/*/ze.conf.resolved

# Runtime / scratch artifacts that leak into the working tree from running ze
/stderr
/stdout
screenlog.*
etc/ze/*.tmp
etc/ze/debug.zefs
# ddos-detect (and other plugins) persist rolling runtime state here; never commit it.
etc/ze/state/
internal/appliance/build/

# Appliance builddir lock for the ze module itself. Derived and duplicated: that
# module is only `replace ze => <repo root>`, so every line of its go.sum is
# already in the root go.sum. The module bytes it would pin are not in the repo
# either (gokrazy/modcache/.gitignore keeps only the gokrazy init source), so
# `make ze-gokrazy-deps` is already a required post-clone step and regenerates
# this file. Tracking it only created a second place to update on every
# dependency bump, and it silently drifted (it still pinned grpc v1.80.0 after
# the root module moved). The other gokrazy/ze/builddir go.sum files stay
# tracked: they pin upstream gokrazy, serial-busybox and rtr7/kernel
# dependencies that appear nowhere else.
gokrazy/ze/builddir/github.com/ze-software/ze/go.sum
